Okay, I've compiled the game with both your patches included and posted
Win32 binaries at:
http://www.hiddenglade.com/download/nh343-hitscroll-suffocate.zip

Notes:
1. Wands of digging do, indeed, expel you from water elementals.
2. The suffocation period seems to be too short for the level
gelatinous cubes appear in the game.  As it is, you get two turns: the
first "you can no longer breathe", the second, "you turn blue," the
third you die.  That's really too short, especially considering that
putting on an amulet of strangulation is considered a bad enough
trouble that your god will step in and uncurse the amulet for you.
3. Hitting a gelatinous cube sometimes paralyzes the player, which is
as a good as an instadeath in this case.

So as it stands, the suffocation attacks are simply too lethal, there
needs to be at least one or two additional turns of leeway, and/or some
further consideration of whether the player is sleeping or paralyzed or
otherwise can't act.

I've not tested out scrolls other than to make sure that the basic
function of the patch works, which it seems to be.

